Project: Two-Stage Lightweight Detection of Indirect Prompt Injection in Tool-Using LLM
An LLM agent reads untrusted content (a web page, an email, a tool output). That content may contain a hidden instruction trying to hijack the agent. We build a two-stage filter that sits in front of the agent:

Stage 1 is a small, fast transformer classifier. It scores every piece of content from 0 (clean) to 1 (injected).
If the score is confidently low or confidently high, we decide immediately. No expensive model is called. This is the common case.
If the score is in the uncertain middle band, we escalate to Stage 2, an LLM that reads the content and gives a verdict.
